{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-5 (c288c917) is built in source at 68397760 on builder/nf5-browser-custody-20261113 (on the final C1 head 5a2a6d82, pushed). Gate order: after C1. Three points need a ruling, and two choices are stated for review.\n\nBuilt:\n- packages/client/src/browser-custody.ts: a `CustodyStore` over IndexedDB, Web Locks and BroadcastChannel, with `byTarget` and the change signal.\n- browser-joining.ts, apps/counter and examples/lending keep their requests in `Custody`. request-custody.ts, request-attempts.ts and request-dispatch.ts are deleted with their exports, and so are Counter's journal.ts and dispatcher.ts.\n- An old-format record is removed when found, and the page shows that the room retired.\n- Terminal records (ruling 72b1d654 item 3): the browser store keeps every unresolved record and the newest 64 terminal records live. A terminal write past 64 moves the oldest terminal record to an archive store in the same transaction. `read` still finds an archived record, and `byTarget` does not list it. Nothing leaves the archive.\nTests on battery, with no timeouts: client custody and browser files 52 passed; Counter Node witnesses 52 passed; Lending 13 passed; type checks clean; security-entry-points 12 passed, with no sealed file changed. The two real-browser files, storage.browser.test.ts in Lending and Counter, typecheck only.\n\nQuestions:\na. examples/lending imported the deleted exports, and c288c917 does not name it. NF-5 moves it onto `Custody` too, because a private copy of `Kept` would contradict \"Kept retires\". Confirm.\nb. Lending's \"Give up\" cannot close a record. `Custody` has no transition for an unresolved record whose latest signing is dead and not found. The page keeps the given-up keys in its own slot and hides those records, but they stay unresolved and count toward the limit of 256. Proposal: settle it in section 6 (\"returned\") of the client note as a separate request, and keep the page's slot until then.\nc. The NF-3 note says NF-5 removes the NF-3 MCP aliases, and c288c917 does not name them. Proposal: remove them in NF-5, or file them as their own small request.\n\nChoices for review:\n- Join: the slot holds `{ v: 2, seat, key }` and is written before signing. The join's custody identity has `membership: null`. `JoinStore.clear(outcome)` names the outcome, so a host can keep the seat of a join that took effect.\n- Counter: a correction signs again under the same key with `resign`, only after `guard-failed` or `revision-moved`.\n\nThe browser witness of the user path is not run yet. It needs a real page with IndexedDB and Web Locks against a real room: lose a join's reply, reload, press Check, and see one join in the journal and the same envelope in custody. Then the same for one Counter act."}